-## Phase 3 Plan: Factories (`spec/fabricators/`) (Next)
-
-Profiling both `spec/models` and `spec/requests` confirmed that built-in factory bloat (untouched in Phases 1 & 2 per instructions) is now the single largest remaining bottleneck across **both** suites (~10–12s in `spec/models` + ~10–12s in `spec/requests`):
-
-1. **`spec/fabricators/status_fabricator.rb` (HIGHEST IMPACT):**
-   - Contains `after_create { |status| Fabricate(:bookmark, status: status) }`!
-   - Every single `Fabricate(:status)` secretly creates a `Bookmark` -> a brand-new `Account` -> a brand-new `User` -> 2 `LoginActivity` records + a BCrypt password hash!
-   - Even *after* Phases 1 & 2 `let_it_be` optimizations, hidden `bookmark` creation still accounts for **410 calls / 4.48s** in `spec/models` and **294 calls / 3.40s** in `spec/requests` (~8s combined!).
-   - Removing this unconditional `after_create` bookmark (adding it only where a spec explicitly needs a bookmark) will roughly halve the cost of `Fabricate(:status)` everywhere.
-2. **`spec/fabricators/user_fabricator.rb`:**
-   - Contains `after_create { |user| 2.times { Fabricate(:login_activity, user: user) } }` — creates 2 unnecessary `LoginActivity` rows on every `User` (and every local `Account`) — still **714 hidden calls** in `spec/requests` and hundreds in `spec/models`.
-   - Uses `password '123456789'`, triggering `BCrypt::Engine.__bc_crypt` (clamped at cost 4, ~1.5ms/call) on every single `User` and local `Account` (~2.0s in `spec/models`, ~1.5s in `spec/requests`). Pre-computing `encrypted_password` once at load time (using `Devise::Encryptor.digest(User, '123456789')`) when `password` is not explicitly overridden will eliminate ~99% of BCrypt CPU time while preserving full password authentication compatibility.
-3. **`spec/fabricators/account_fabricator.rb`:**
-   - Every local `Account` builds & persists an associated `User` (`user { |attrs| attrs[:domain].nil? ? Fabricate.build(:user, account: nil) : nil }`), which runs `User#set_approved` (`UsernameBlock.matches?`, `EmailDomainBlock.requires_approval?`, `UserRole.everyone`, `UnreservedUsernameValidator`, `UniqueUsernameValidator`), BCrypt, and 2x `LoginActivity`.
-   - Optimizing `user_fabricator` immediately speeds up every local `Account`, and auditing whether some specs/fabricators even need a `User` for every local `Account` can save even more.
-4. **`spec/fabricators/media_attachment_fabricator.rb`:**
-   - Attaches real fixture files (`attachment.jpg` / `attachment.webm`) and runs Paperclip/Vips/Blurhash/FFmpeg processing on every `Fabricate(:media_attachment)` (~5s in `spec/models`, ~1.3s in `spec/requests`). Consider lightweight/stubbed variants or traits where specs only need a persisted `MediaAttachment` record without actual image transcoding.
-5. **`spec/fabricators/accessible_access_token_fabricator.rb`:**
-   - Consider setting a default `last_used_at { Time.now.utc }` (or in `access_token_fabricator.rb` where tests don't explicitly test `last_used_at: nil`) so any future request spec outside `'with API authentication'` also avoids `AccessTokenTrackingConcern` `UPDATE` writes on every request.
+## Phase 3: Factories (`spec/fabricators/`) & Factory Usage (Completed)
+
+### Summary of Results
+
+Starting from the post-Phase-2 baseline measured in the same environment:
+
+| Suite | Phase 3 Baseline | Phase 3 Final | Phase 3 Improvement | SQL Queries (`sql.active_record`) | Factory Calls (total / top-level) | Factory Time (`FPROF`) |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **`spec/models`** (1,795 exs) | **32.74s** (seed 18415) | **18.9s – 23.8s (~20.5s)** | **-37% (~1.6x faster)** | **41,889 -> 28,123 (-32.9%)** | **2,540 / 1,763 -> 1,808 / 1,714** | **21.61s -> 12.66s (-41.4%)** |
+| **`spec/requests`** (1,877 exs) | **44.06s** (seed 23323) | **30.35s – 33.91s (~32.0s)** | **-27% (~1.38x faster)** | **65,363 -> 50,883 (-22.2%)** | **2,914 / 1,870 -> 1,517 / 1,474 (-47.9%)** | **17.36s -> 8.41s (-51.6%)** |
+| **Combined (`models` + `requests`)** | **76.80s** | **~52.5s** (best: **49.3s**) | **-32% (~1.46x faster)** | **107,252 -> 79,006 (-26.3%)** | **5,454 -> 3,325 (-39.0%)** | **38.97s -> 21.07s (-45.9%)** |
+
+Cumulative improvement across all 3 phases vs original baseline:
+- `spec/models`: **124.1s -> ~20.5s** (**~6.0x faster**, -83.5%)
+- `spec/requests`: **161.2s (post-Phase-1; >250s pre-Phase-1) -> ~32.0s** (**~5.0x faster vs post-Phase-1**, ~7.8x vs pre-Phase-1)
+- **Combined (`spec/models` + `spec/requests`)**: **>375s original -> ~52.5s** (**>7x faster overall**).
+
+### Root Causes Found & Fixed in Phase 3
+
+1. **Hidden nested `after_create` fabrications in core fabricators (~7.5s combined)**
+   - `spec/fabricators/status_fabricator.rb`: removed unconditional `after_create { |status| Fabricate(:bookmark, status: status) }`, which secretly created a `Bookmark` + `Account` + `User` + `Keypair` + BCrypt hash + 16 SQL queries on every `Fabricate(:status)` (410 hidden calls in `spec/models`, 285 in `spec/requests`). Drops `Fabricate(:status, account: existing_acc)` from **11.9ms / 19 queries -> ~1ms / 3 queries**.
+   - `spec/fabricators/user_fabricator.rb`: removed unconditional `after_create { |user| 2.times { Fabricate(:login_activity, user: user) } }` (206 hidden calls in `spec/models`, 714 in `spec/requests`).
+   - `spec/fabricators/status_trend_fabricator.rb`: reused `status.account` / `account` instead of fabricating two separate `Account` + `User` pairs per `StatusTrend`.
+   - `spec/fabricators/notification_request_fabricator.rb`: passed `account: attrs[:from_account]` to `last_status` instead of fabricating a third unrelated `Account`.
+   - `spec/fabricators/announcement_reaction_fabricator.rb`: defaulted `name` to `'😀'` instead of fabricating a `CustomEmoji` (which previously ran ImageMagick/Paperclip).
+
+2. **Repeated BCrypt password hashing on every `User` and local `Account` (~3s combined)**
+   - `spec/fabricators/user_fabricator.rb`: lazily precomputed `Devise::Encryptor.digest(User, '123456789')` once per RSpec process and set `encrypted_password` directly with `transient password: '123456789'`, populating `@password` via `after_build` so `user.password`, `valid_password?('123456789')`, Devise `Validatable`, explicit `password:` overrides, and `encrypted_password: ''` overrides all behave identically.
+   - Reduced StackProf `BCrypt::Engine.__bc_crypt` samples by **>92%** in `spec/models` (1,838 -> 149) and eliminated it completely from top frames in `spec/requests` (1,290 -> negligible).
+
+3. **Unnecessary `Keypair` table writes + `ActiveRecord::Encryption` + 2048-bit RSA keygen (~3–4s combined)**
+   - `spec/fabricators/account_fabricator.rb`: defaulted local accounts (`domain.nil?`) to legacy `public_key` / `private_key` (unless `with_keypair: true` is passed), skipping 2 `SELECT keypairs` uniqueness checks, 1 `INSERT INTO keypairs`, and `ActiveRecord::Encryption` AES-256-GCM + `Zlib.deflate` on `Keypair#private_key` (~1.3–2.1ms saved per local account/user). `Account#keypair` falls back transparently via `Keypair.from_legacy_account(self)`. Remote accounts keep their `keypairs` association untouched for `Keypair.from_keyid` / ActivityPub signature specs.
+   - `spec/fabricators/keypair_fabricator.rb`: changed `Fabricate(:account, keypairs: [])` (which triggered `Account#generate_keys` -> 46ms 2048-bit RSA generation!) to `Fabricate(:account, legacy_keypair: true)`.
+
+4. **Real Paperclip / Vips / ImageMagick / FFmpeg processing in default fabricators (~2.5s combined)**
+   - `spec/fabricators/preview_card_fabricator.rb`: omitted `image` by default (added `transient with_image: false`; enabled `with_image: true` in `spec/lib/vacuum/preview_cards_vacuum_spec.rb` and `spec/lib/mastodon/cli/preview_cards_spec.rb`). Drops `Fabricate(:preview_card)` from **71ms -> 0.8ms** (~90x faster).
+   - `spec/fabricators/custom_emoji_fabricator.rb`: populated Paperclip metadata columns (`image_file_name`, `image_content_type`, `image_file_size`, `image_updated_at`) directly by default (added `transient image: :__default__, with_image: false`; enabled `with_image: true` in `spec/models/form/custom_emoji_batch_spec.rb` copy test and `spec/lib/mastodon/cli/emoji_spec.rb` export test). Drops `Fabricate(:custom_emoji)` from **40ms -> 0.8ms** (~50x faster).
+   - `spec/fabricators/media_attachment_fabricator.rb`: populated Paperclip columns/metadata (`file_file_name`, `file_content_type`, `file_file_size`, `file_meta`, `blurhash`, `processing`, `file_storage_schema_version`) directly by default when neither `file:` nor `with_file: true` is passed (enabled `with_file: true` in `spec/requests/public_files_spec.rb`, `spec/services/backup_service_spec.rb`, and `spec/lib/mastodon/cli/media_spec.rb`). Drops default `Fabricate(:media_attachment)` from **114ms -> ~1ms** (plus account).
+
+5. **`Faker` YAML parsing at boot & runtime (~1.0s combined)**
+   - `spec/fabricators/web_push_subscription_fabricator.rb` previously called `Faker::Internet.url` eagerly at file load time, forcing `Psych::Parser` to parse Faker YAML locales (~280ms) on every RSpec boot. Also memoized EC `prime256v1` `key_p256dh` generation.
+   - Replaced `Faker::*` calls across `spec/fabricators/` (`account`, `user`, `status`, `tag`, `preview_card`, `domain_block`, `email_domain_block`, `fasp/provider`, `terms_of_service`, etc.) with fast deterministic sequences/strings, eliminating `Psych::Parser#_native_parse` from StackProf.
+
+6. **Default `last_used_at` on `:accessible_access_token`**
+   - `spec/fabricators/accessible_access_token_fabricator.rb`: added `last_used_at { Time.now.utc }` so tokens created outside `'with API authentication'` also avoid `AccessTokenTrackingConcern` `UPDATE oauth_access_tokens` writes on every request.
+
+7. **Factory usage & shared setup improvements across top remaining slow specs**
+   - **`spec/models` (12 files):**
+     - `media_attachment_spec.rb`: switched `needs_redownload?` from animated `avatar.gif` (2x 290ms = 580ms!) to `mini-static.gif`, and `size limit validation` positive cases from `Fabricate` to `Fabricate.build`.
+     - `account/avatar_spec.rb` & `account/header_spec.rb`: shared `let_it_be(:account)` for read-only base64 attachment specs.
+     - `trends/statuses_spec.rb`, `notification_spec.rb`, `status_spec.rb`, `public_feed_spec.rb`, `report_spec.rb`, `fasp/backfill_request_spec.rb`, `concerns/account/mappings_spec.rb`, `export_spec.rb`, `featured_tag_spec.rb`: reused shared `let_it_be` accounts across multi-status / multi-action_log / multi-notification setups instead of implicitly fabricating dozens of throwaway `Account` + `User` pairs.
+   - **`spec/requests` (33 files):**
+     - Standardized `api/v1/directories_spec.rb`, `api/v1/follow_requests_spec.rb`, `api/v1/emails/confirmations_spec.rb`, and `api/v1/statuses/contexts_spec.rb` onto `'with API authentication'` / `user_attributes:` (eliminating redundant per-example `User` + `AccessToken` creation).
+     - Converted shared resource `let`s to `let_it_be` / `before_all` across top factory-heavy & `forbidden for wrong scope`/`role` specs (`api/v2/search_spec.rb`, `signature_verification_spec.rb`, `well_known/webfinger_spec.rb`, `api/v1/accounts/{follower_accounts,following_accounts,relationships}_spec.rb`, `activitypub/{followers_synchronizations,inboxes}_spec.rb`, `api/v1/{collections,in_collections,collection_items,lists,lists/accounts,blocks,favourites,mutes,bookmarks,reports,tags}_spec.rb`, `api/v2/{filters,filters/statuses}_spec.rb`, `api/v1/admin/{domain_blocks,domain_allows,email_domain_blocks,tags,trends/links/links}_spec.rb`, `admin/{accounts,collections,roles}_spec.rb`).
+
+### Phase 3 Gotchas Discovered
+
+- **Local `Account` MUST have an associated `User` in Mastodon:**
+  Testing `user: nil` on child fabricators (`status`, `report`, `account_stat`) passed all 1,795 model specs but broke request specs (`activitypub/replies_spec.rb`, `admin/reports_spec.rb`, `api/v1/directories_spec.rb`, `api/v1/statuses_spec.rb`) because Mastodon controllers/scopes check `account.user_approved?` / `without_unapproved` (which joins `:user`). Always keep `Account` -> `User` intact for local accounts; reduce `User` overhead instead by sharing `let_it_be(:account)` records and optimizing `user_fabricator`.
+- **Remote `Account` must keep `public_key: ''` and `keypairs` by default:**
+  `spec/models/keypair_spec.rb` asserts `Keypair.from_keyid` returns `nil` when a remote account has no matching keypair and no legacy `public_key`, and `spec/lib/activitypub/linked_data_signature_spec.rb` / `spec/services/activitypub/process_account_service_spec.rb` call `account.keypairs.delete_all` on remote accounts. Defaulting to legacy keypair only for *local* accounts (`domain.nil?`) preserves full compatibility across the entire suite.
+- **Devise `@password` + Fabrication `transient password:`:**
+  Specs calling `user.password` (e.g. `POST /auth/sign_in` in request/controller/system specs) and Devise `Validatable` (`validates_presence_of :password` on create) require `@password` to be populated even when `encrypted_password` is precomputed. Setting `user.instance_variable_set(:@password, default_user_password)` inside `after_build` when `transients[:password] == default_user_password` handles default users, `encrypted_password: ''`, custom `password: '...'`, and `external: true, password: nil` cleanly.
+- **Paperclip metadata-only fabricators:**
+  Setting `file_file_name`, `file_content_type`, `file_file_size`, `file_meta`, `blurhash`, `processing`, and `file_storage_schema_version` directly passes Paperclip validations and generates valid URLs/JSON without touching disk, Vips, or FFmpeg. Only the handful of specs that read/serve/stat/copy/export the physical file on disk need `with_file: true` / `with_image: true`.
+
+### Current Remaining Profile Snapshot
+
+- **`spec/models` (~20.5s total):**
+  - `spec/models/media_attachment_spec.rb`: **~4.2s** (mostly `boop.mp3` ffmpeg transcoding = 2.64s + real format transcoding tests).
+  - Remaining factories: **~8.8s** across 1,787 non-media calls (`account`, `status`, `user`), now pure ActiveRecord + PostgreSQL (~5.4ms per local `Account`+`User` pair).
+  - Test execution + assertions across 1,795 examples: **~7.5s**.
+- **`spec/requests` (~32.0s total):**
+  - Factories: **8.41s** (~26% of runtime, down from 17.36s in Phase 3 baseline and 103.8s in Phase 2 baseline!).
+  - Actual HTTP request execution (`ActionDispatch` -> Controller -> Serializer/View -> PostgreSQL) across 1,877 examples: **~23s** (~12ms/request).
